Red Hat CSAF VEX Important
litellm: LiteLLM: Unauthorized access due to authentication bypass
known affected: 1 known not affected: 8
Vendor statement: affects LiteLLM proxy deployments prior to 1.84.0 where the MCP Streamable HTTP endpoint is exposed. Red Hat products that include LiteLLM as a Python dependency— including Red Hat OpenShift AI (odh-mlflow-rhel9 and similar images), Red Hat Ansible Automation Platform Lightspeed chatbot images (lightspeed-chatbot-rhel9, ansible-chatbot-stack), and Red Hat Exploit Intelligence (vulnerability-analysis-rhel9)—are not affected in their default configurations because they do not start the LiteLLM proxy server or expose its MCP HTTP authentication path. These images run services such as MLflow, Lightspeed Core (lightspeed_stack.py), or vulnerability analysis workloads and use LiteLLM only as a client library or transitive dependency. The vulnerable execute path is reachable only when LiteLLM proxy is explicitly deployed with MCP routes enabled.
